# Line endings are handled by git for everyone, independent of personal settings (core.autocrlf etc.):
# - text files are stored with LF in the repository,
# - on checkout they get the platform's native line ending (CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux/macOS),
# - on commit any CRLF/LF mix an editor or tool produced is normalized again.
# So nobody needs to care about line endings in their editor; diffs never show line ending changes.
# Git detects text vs. binary by itself; the binary list below only makes sure for common formats.
* text=auto

# Need a fixed line ending regardless of platform
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

*.cs   text diff=csharp

# Binary (never converted, no text diff)
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.bmp    binary
*.ico    binary
*.dds    binary
